.\" acompat.3 -- libacompat (libamixcompat), userland/packages/acompat.
.\" BSD-2-Clause, see acompat/LICENSE.
.TH ACOMPAT 3 "2026-10-30" "acompat 0.1" "Amix add-on libraries"
.SH NAME
acompat \- libamixcompat, the C library functions and headers Amix lacks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <amixcompat.h>
.PP
.BI "int snprintf(char *" str ", size_t " size ", const char *" format ", ...);"
.BI "int vsnprintf(char *" str ", size_t " size ", const char *" format ", va_list " ap );
.BI "int setenv(const char *" name ", const char *" value ", int " overwrite );
.BI "int unsetenv(const char *" name );
.BI "int strcasecmp(const char *" s1 ", const char *" s2 );
.BI "int strncasecmp(const char *" s1 ", const char *" s2 ", size_t " n );
.BI "int mkstemp(char *" template );
.BI "int usleep(unsigned int " usec );
.BI "int gettimeofday(struct timeval *" tp ", void *" tzp );
.B "const char *amix_compat_version(void);"
.PP
.B #include <stdint.h>
.B #include <strings.h>
.PP
.B cc \-I/usr/local/include ... \-L/usr/local/lib \-lacompat
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B libacompat
is a static library of the C library functions the Amix (SVR4.0) libc does not
have, with the headers that declare them.
Each one was measured absent from
.BR /usr/lib/libc.so.1 .
The archive is named
.B libacompat.a
because the s5 root file system keeps 14 bytes of a name, and
.B libamixcompat.a
is 15.
.TP
.BR snprintf ", " vsnprintf
C99 formatted output into a buffer of
.I size
bytes, always terminated, returning the length the full output would have.
They handle the
.BR ll ,
.BR j ,
.B z
and
.B t
length modifiers, so 64-bit integers print correctly; the stock
.BR printf (3S)
has no
.B ll
modifier.
Floating-point conversions are done by the stock
.BR sprintf (3S),
and need a 68881 or 68882.
.B %n
is not implemented: it is printed as written.
A null string prints as
.BR (null) ,
truncated by a precision; a null pointer prints as
.BR 0x0 .
.TP
.BR setenv ", " unsetenv
Add, change or remove an environment variable; the strings are copied.
.TP
.BR strcasecmp ", " strncasecmp
Compare strings ignoring ASCII case.
.TP
.B mkstemp
Replace the trailing
.B XXXXXX
of
.I template
and create the file exclusively, mode 0600; returns its descriptor.
.TP
.B usleep
Sleep for
.I usec
microseconds, rounded up to the clock tick; built on
.BR poll (2),
so it leaves the caller's timers alone.
.TP
.B gettimeofday
The time of day, seconds and microseconds, from the stock one-argument
.BR _abi_gettimeofday ;
.I tzp
is ignored.
.TP
.B amix_compat_version
The library's version string, e.g.
.BR 0.1\-7\-gcc14 .
.PP
.B <stdint.h>
gives the exact-width integer types of this ILP32 big-endian target, and
.B <strings.h>
declares
.B strcasecmp
and
.B strncasecmp
only; neither header exists on a stock system.
.B <amixcompat.h>
also defines
.BR ssize_t .
.SH RETURN VALUE
.B snprintf
and
.B vsnprintf
return the length the output would have had, or \-1 with
.I errno
set to ENOMEM when a floating-point conversion cannot get its buffer.
.BR setenv ,
.BR unsetenv ,
.B usleep
and
.B gettimeofday
return 0, or \-1 with
.I errno
set.
.B mkstemp
returns a file descriptor, or \-1.
.SH NOTES
Do not compile with
.B \-ansi
or
.BR \-D_POSIX_SOURCE :
many Amix headers hide declarations in their ANSI view, among them
.BR "struct timeval" ,
which
.B gettimeofday
needs.
.PP
.B strcasecmp
is absent from libc but present in
.BR libresolv.a ,
declared in no system header.
Linking both
.B \-lresolv
and
.BR \-lacompat ,
the archive the linker reaches first wins; both agree on ASCII.
.PP
Programs built with GCC 14 get these functions from the toolchain's own
runtime, and do not link
.BR libacompat .
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /usr/local/lib/libacompat.a
The library.
.TP
.B /usr/local/include/{amixcompat.h,stdint.h,strings.h}
The headers.
.TP
.B /usr/local/bin/acompat-test
The on-box acceptance test,
.BR acompat\-test (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR acompat\-test (1)
